    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001059 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001059">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which a signifier of a quality is expressed as a multitude or magnitude.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Zeichen einer Eigenschaft als eine Menge, Größe oder ein Ausmaß ausgedrückt wird.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref xml:lang="de">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantification_%28science%29</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Quantifizierung</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">quantification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">count</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">measurement</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Quantifikationsprozess</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">quantification process</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A process during which a signal or phenomenon is expressed as a multitude or magnitude.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Prozess, bei dem ein Signal oder ein Phänomen als eine Menge,  Größe oder ein Ausmaß ausgedrückt wird.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Quantifizierungsprozesse</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">quantification processes</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001060 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001060">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A signifier which is the output of a quantification process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Zeichen, das das Ergebnis eines Quantifizierungsprozesses ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">During a quantification process an agent perceives a type of count quality which acts is then transformed into an output in form of a signifier of an quantity.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Zeichen einer Quantiät</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">signifier of a quantity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001061 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001061">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002233"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002234"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which an agent perceives some quality and creates a signifier thereof.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Akteur eine Eigenschaft wahrnimmt und davon ein Zeichen erschafft.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">this class could have subclass axioms added: has participant some agent. For this class agent needs to be defined or imported. This could also be done at the instance level where the nature of the agent can be identified more clearly (i.e. machine agent, human or else).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This is the process which creates a generically dependent contiinuant that represents a specifically dependent continuant.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">We need to think about how to deal with the &quot;perception process&quot;. Is it the same as the qualification process, or do we need a new class?</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Qualifizierungsprozess</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">qualification process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001066 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001066">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A function which inheres in a bearer and is realised when that bearer allows to estimate the existence, identity, properties, or behaviours of an entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Funktion, die einem Träger innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn dieser Träger es ermöglicht, die Existenz, die Identität, die Eigenschaften oder das Verhalten einer Entität zu schätzen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Modell Funktion</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">model function</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Under colloquial use, entities that bear the model function are often referred to as &quot;the model&quot;. Also, colloquially the term model is also used as a verb in order to express the process of (computational) modelling, e.g. &quot;i am going to model phenomenon xyz&quot;).

The bearer might be material entities such as a scale model of a car, or a generically dependent continuant such as a mathematical formula that models a process. The estimation of properties may be in past (e.g. estimation of the temperature during the big bang), present (estimation of the proportions of a car through a scale model, or the prediction of a parameter based on others) or the future (estimation of a neurons membrane potential in a network). 

Models are always an abstraction of the entity that they represent. A differential equation can be used to simulate the membrane potential  of a neuron over time while the spatial extend and complexity of the neuron itself is reduced to a point process. Further models highly depend on input parameters partly determining the behavior of the model and as such are often loaded with assumptions. In that sense the model output is an estimation that can be interpreted by an agent in order to infer or indicate information about another entity (i.e. existence or else).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Modell</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001067 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001067">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001066"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000056"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001068"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A model which is formalised in order to be executed or resolved.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Modell, das formalisiert wird, um ausgeführt oder gelöst zu werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Computermodell Funktion</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computational model function</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computergestütztes Modell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The bearer of the computational model might be a mathematical formula such as a differential equation (e.g. predicting dynamics of a parameter over some dimension such as time). A model may be used in a process such as a computational modelling to generate simulation data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Computermodell</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">computational model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001068 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001068">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001067"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which a computational model is executed or resolved to estimate the existence, identity, properties or behaviour of an entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Computermodell ausgeführt oder aufgelöst wird, um die Existenz, die Identität, die Eigenschaften oder das Verhalten einer Entität abzuschätzen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">simulation</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computational simulation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computergestützte Simluation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">computational modelling</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">computergestützte Modellierung</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001069 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001069">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000042"/>
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000112"/>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Quantitative Daten, die das Ergebnis einer computergestützten Simulation sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Quantitative data which are the output of computational modelling.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">computation data</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">computational data</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">simulation data</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">simulational data</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">simulation data</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001070 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001070">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001059"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">A quantification process during which the quantified signifier of a quality stems from an independent continuant.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Quantifizierungsprozess, bei dem der zu quantifizierte Signifier einer Qualität von einem Independent Continuant abhängt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Messung</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">measurement</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class is created to differentiate quantification processes in real-world (= physical) entities that can be measured (i.e. with a tape measure, versus these quantification processes that happen during calculations or computational modelling. Independent continuants  encompass material entities (e.g. physical objects) as well as immaterial entities (e.g. the border of a country).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Messprozess</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">measurement process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001071 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001071">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000112"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class is created to be able to discriminate data originating from computational models (HDO_00001069) from those that comes from measurements and experimentation (this class).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Messdaten</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">measurement data</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Messdaten</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">Quantitative data which are the output of a measurement process.</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">measurement data</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001072 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001072">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000007"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">providing a workshop to participants</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">providing space to storage</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">A planned process during which an agent performs a task for another one.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Agent eine Aufgabe für einen anderen Agenten ausführt</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">services</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Service</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">service</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001073 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001073">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A quality which inheres in an entity, by virtue of its properties being defined in a specification which is not publicly released.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Qualität, die einer Entität dadurch innerwohnt, dass ihre Eigenschaften in einer Spezifikation definiert sind, die nicht öffentlich zugänglich ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">proprietary</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">proprietär</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">proprietariness</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001074 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001074">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A file format which is proprietary.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Dateiformat, welches proprietär ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C85871</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_file_format</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_file_format#Prominent_proprietary_formats</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Proprietary formats are typically used by instrument and/or software vendors to store and process data in specific (e.g. efficient, or intentionally inaccessible) ways for a given application. Intentional or not, data encoding in proprietary data formats - to which the specification is unknown - typically results in data and metadata access being impaired or impossible. There are cases where proprietary data formats were opened after some time, i.e when introducing a new version of the proprietary specification. Examples of open proprietary formats are doc and mp3.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Proprietäres Dateiformat</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">proprietary file format</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001075 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001075">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">OBSOLETE Information which identifies the copyrights a resource is released under.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">OBSOLETE Informationen welche identifizieren unter welchen Urheberrechten eine Ressource freigegeben ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:consider rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">copyright statement</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>This is class is obsolete because we decided to integrate it as an object property 
that relates the class &apos;copyright&apos; to an entity.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">obsolete Copyright Information</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete copyright information</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Legal right which inheres in an entity by virtue of being the owner, creator or inventor of another entity, and which permits the first entity to (1) copy, alter, delete, or reuse the other entity and to (2) pass on copyrights in full or partially to a third entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Recht, das einer Entität dadurch zusteht, dass es Eigentümer, Schöpfer oder Erfinder einer anderen Entität ist, und das (1) das Kopieren, Verändern, Löschen oder Wiederverwenden dieser Entität, und (2) die vollständige oder teilweise Weitergabe der Urheberrechte an eine dritte Entität erlaubt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Copyright</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">copright information</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">copyright statement</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Copyright is intended to secure the ideal and commercial interest of an entity over its intellectual property. That is typically an entity being the creator of another entity, for example the author typically holds the copyright for a text written by him/her.
In research, expecially in cases of research data that is recorded in large infrastructures copyright is often not held soly by the creator of the data but also by the insittution where the data was recorded, the owner of the instruments that were used to record the data, or else. In these cases copyright might and should be pre-determined through explicit agreement (e.g. within employment or usage contracts) and be made explicit through licnensing of the data.
Copyright is a legal matter, and this class and its definition are not authoritative.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Urheberrecht</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">copyright</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001077 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001077">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001017"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000029"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001023"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A digital system which comprises structured data, (meta)data, and software and which allows a computer to store, organise, and access structured data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein digitales System welches aus strukturierten Daten, (Meta)daten und Software besteht und das es einem Computer erlaubt, strukturierte Daten zu speichern, zu organisieren und auf diese zuzugreifen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:source rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_system"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Metadata stored in a file system is associated with files and may include the file name, the length of the contents of a file, and the location of the file in the folder hierarchy—separate from the contents of the file. A file system differs from other forms of data management systems (e.g a database management system) in that file systems supports and/or requires, e.g., filenames, filename extensions, magic numbers, and other unique components. These components result in markedly different user experiences when accessing structured data through such systems.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Dateisystem</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">file system</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A specification which defines how data is to be serialized as a defined unit for handling within a file system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation, die festlegt, wie Daten als definierte Einheit für die Handhabung in einem Dateisystem serialisiert werden sollen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A file format specifies serialization for storage. There are data formats like XML, JSON that can be stored with file name extensions and therefore might in practice be used in the sense of a file format.

On a hardware-level, parts of a file might be stored in different locations in a discontinuous fashion. Typically files follow a defined file format to be usable by software and may include a file signature that minimally identifies the file format. Files are typically handled with some file system. For digital files that would typically be the file system of the operating system.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Dateiformat</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">file format</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A vocabulary which only includes terms that have been deliberately selected by its authors and/or maintainers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, welches nur Begriffe enthält, die mit Absicht durch die Verantwortlichen ausgewählt wurden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Controlled_vocabulary"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Controlled_vocabulary#In_library_and_information_science"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The methodology used to construct a controlled vocabulary should be documented to verify that the term collection is indeed controlled by it. Controlled vocabularies should address the issues with homographs, synonyms and polysemes by a bijection between concepts and authorized terms. In short, controlled vocabularies reduce ambiguity inherent in normal human language where the same concept can be given different names and ensure consistency.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">controlled vocabulary</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">kontrolliertes Vokabular</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A vocabulary which only includes terms that have been deliberately selected by its creators or maintainers. </skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, welches nur Begriffe enthält, die durch die Verantwortlichen gezielt ausgewählt wurden.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002006"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A terminology which associates terms with explanations of their meanings (i.e. glosses).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Terminologie, die Begriffe mit Erläuterungen zu ihrer Bedeutung (ihren Glossen) verbindet.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Begriffserklärung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://inmyownterms.com/is-this-a-glossary-a-lexicon-or-a-thesaurus-how-to-tell-them-apart/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Glossar</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">glossary</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A collection of terms with corresponding explanations of their meanings (i.e. their glosses).</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Sammlung von Begriffen mit den dazugehörenden Erläuterungen zu deren Bedeutung (ihre Glosse).</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Glossare</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">glossaries</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A vocabulary which is structured.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, das strukturiert ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://inmyownterms.com/is-this-a-glossary-a-lexicon-or-a-thesaurus-how-to-tell-them-apart/"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Please see the definition of &quot;structure&quot;. Note that the mentioned structure does not necessarily reflect strict semantic relationships, as it may simply be functional (for a user interface) or convenience grouping. Relations may be encoded as simple as whitespace indentation in a list, or in more complex forms using RDF predicates. The structure could be defined by additional syntax around the terms such as OWL restrictions or SKOS assertions - it can differ depending on implementation. TODO: see discussion at https://gitlab.hzdr.de/hmc/hmc/cct-7-semantics/hmc-glossary-initialization/-/merge_requests/88</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">structured vocabulary</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">strukturiertes Vokabular</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A vocabulary in which terms are arranged to represent some relationship between them, e.g. hierarchical nesting, to indicates broader or narrower meanings of terms.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, in dem die Begriffe so angeordnet sind, dass sie in einer bestimmten Beziehung zueinander stehen, z. B. durch hierarchische Verschachtelung, um um die weitere oder eingeschränkte Bedeutung der Begriffe darzustellen.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Structured data which has structuredness conforming to a taxonomy specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Strukturierte Daten, deren Strukturiertheit einer Taxonomiespezifikation entspricht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://inmyownterms.com/is-this-a-glossary-a-lexicon-or-a-thesaurus-how-to-tell-them-apart/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taxonomy"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hierarchical arrangement of objects based on how similar they are to one another.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Eine hierarchische Unterteilung von Objekten, basierend auf ihrer Ähnlichkeit.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Entities deeper in the hierarchy need to retain all the properties of their ancestors. Terminologies can also be structured in taxonomy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Need to be revised to differentiate taxonomical data from taxonomy itself</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Taxonomische Daten</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">taxonomical data</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Taxonomien</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">taxonomies</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000046"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A string which is associated with a meaning.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Zeichenfolge, die mit einer Bedeutung assoziiert ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/term"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1969448"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Benennung</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Fachbegriff</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Fachwort</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Terminus</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">disciplinary term</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">technical term</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">expression</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">word</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Terms can be single words or multi-word phrases. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Begriff</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">term</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A word or phrase which is associated with a meaning intended to describe something or someone.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Wort oder ein Ausdruck, der mit einer Bedeutung assoziert wird die etwas oder jemanden beschreibt.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Begriffe</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">terms</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002006 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002006">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A vocabulary which is composed of terms used in a domain of knowledge.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, das sich aus Begriffen zusammensetzt, die in einem Wissensgebiet verwendet werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-688X"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Nomenklatur</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">nomenclature</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Fachjargon</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">jargon</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Because &quot;terminology&quot; also pertains to the study of terms, it&apos;s sometimes used as a broad class to refer to thesauri, ontologies, etc as they are often the output of this study.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Terminologie</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">terminology</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A vocabulary which includes terms used within a community or a discipline.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Vokabular, das Begriffe enthält, die innerhalb einer Disziplin verwendet werden.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Terminologien</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">terminologies</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002007 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002007">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002006"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A terminology which relates terms to one another based on their synonymy or antonymy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Terminologie, die Begriffe auf der Grundlage ihrer Synonymie oder Antonymie miteinander in Beziehung setzt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thesaurus_(disambiguation)"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Thesauri often use types of synonymy or antonymy to relate terms to one another, and are often digitally encoded in SKOS. Thesauri may or may not include definitions, in which case they include a glossary as a part.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Thesaurus</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">thesaurus</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A terminology in which terms are associated with their synonyms and antonyms.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Eine Terminologie, in der Begriffe mit ihren Synonymen und Antonymen in Beziehung gesetzt werden.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Thesauren</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Thesauri</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">thesauri</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">thesauruses</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A semantic artefact which comprises a collection of terms.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datensatz der aus einer Sammlung von Begriffen besteht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://inmyownterms.com/is-this-a-glossary-a-lexicon-or-a-thesaurus-how-to-tell-them-apart/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.duden.de/rechtschreibung/Vokabular"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Wortschatz</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Vocabularies in general might not always be recorded or written down explicitly -  within the scope of HDO, this is seen as a sematic artefact and therefore data.within the scope.
Vocabularies are arbitrarily bounded, but are often restricted to a discipline or area of interest. Technically a vocabulary can consist of 2 terms or more.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Vokabular</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">vocabulary</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A collection of terms.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Eine Sammlung von Begriffen.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Vokabulare</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">vocabularies</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002009 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002009">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002010"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A plan specification pertaining to the handling of data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Planungsspezifikation, die Ziel- und Handlungsvorgaben umfasst, die den Umgang mit Daten betreffen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:OMO_0003012 xml:lang="de">DMP</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <obo:OMO_0003012 xml:lang="en">DMP</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4322-180X"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://codata.org/rdm-glossary/data-management-plan/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.forschungsdaten.info/themen/informieren-und-planen/datenmanagementplan/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">research data management plan</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Data management plans often conform to standardised templates, however, many are ad hoc or informal.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenmanagementplan</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data management plan</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A guide describing a series of steps needed to handle data to meet one or more aims. For research data, a data management plan specifies what measures will be taken throughout and often beyond a research project to ensure that its data is well documented, findable, accessible, and reusable.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Leitfaden, der eine Reihe von Schritten beschreibt, welche im Umgang mit Daten erforderlich sind, um eins oder mehrere Ziele zu erreichen. Im Falle von wissenschaflichen Daten legt ein Datenmanagementplan fest, welche Maßnahmen ergriffen werden sollen um sicherzustellen, dass diese Daten, während und nach einem Projekt, dokumentiert, auffindbar, zugänglich und wiederverwendbar sind. </skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Datenmanagementpläne</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">data management plans</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Datenmanagementplan</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">data management plan</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002010 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002010">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A specification which (1) includes objective specifications and action specifications and (2) is intended to guide agents participating in a process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation, die (1) Ziel- und Handlungsvorgaben beinhaltet und (2) darauf ausgelegt ist, an einem Prozess Beteiligte zu leiten. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This is an HMC variation of an ontological definition from the Information Artifact Ontology, set in alignment to the Basic Formal Ontology&apos;s treatment of generically and specifically dependent continuants. We do not include the notions of concretisation or realisation here, but may move towards them in more expressive adaptations of this thesaurus.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Planungsspezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">plan specification</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A description of steps which can be followed to fulfill one or more objectives.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Eine Beschreibung von Schritten, die es ermöglichen, ein Ziel zu erreichen.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002011 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002011">
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A permission which is legally binding, and minimally specifies (1) the parties involved in the permission, (2) one or more entities for which the permission is being made, and (3) a list of rights one party (the licensor) grants to the other (the licensee) over the entities governed by the permission.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Genehmigung die rechtlich bindend ist und mindestens (1) die beteiligten Parteien, (2) eine oder mehrerer Entitäten, für die die Genehmigung gilt und (3) die Rechte, die eine Partei (Lizenzgeber) der anderen (Lizenznehmer) über die in der Lizenz erfassten Entitäten gewährt, spezifiziert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/swo/SWO_0000002"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/License"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://spdx.org/licenses/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">license</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Lizenzvereinbarung</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">licence agreement</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>A license agreement over digital assets or research outputs, in most cases, is a contract/agreement between the copyright holder of a resource (licensor) and a licensee who wants to use and/or redistribute this resource. A number of standard license-agreements can be found prepared in an ready-to-apply state on the web, such as the creative commons licenses (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/2.5/) or MIT lincense (https://opensource.org/license/mit/). 
Licensing is a legal matter, and this class and its definition are not authoritative.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Lizenz</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">license</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A license agreement is a legal instrument in which a legal entity grants rights over a protected work - such as those allowing usage, duplication, and redistribution - to another legal entity.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Eine Lizenzvereinbarung ist ein Rechtsinstrument, durch das eine juristische Person einer anderen juristischen Person bestimmte Rechte an einem geschützten Werk - wie Nutzungs-, Vervielfältigungs- und Weiterverbreitungsrechte - gewährt.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002012 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002012">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Information which identifies a license agreement that applies to a resource.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Information, die angibt, unter welche Lizenzvereinbarung eine Ressource veröffentlicht wurde.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/swo/SWO_0000002"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/License"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://spdx.org/licenses/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">licence information</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">licensing information</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Lizenz</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">licence</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">license</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This term pertains to the actual (meta)data used to identify the licensing agreement pertaining to a digital asset. It does not refer to the license agreement itself, which is a legal agreement. Thus information like (1) the string &quot;CC-BY&quot; as the value of a key &quot;license&quot; in a metadata set or (2) a corresponding logo issued by the licensing authority is license information, whereas the full text of the CC-BY NC 2.5 license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/2.5/) is the actual license agreement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Lizenzinformation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">license information</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Die Lizenzinformationen geben durch Text, Code oder andere beschreibende Elemente an, unter welcher Lizenz eine Ressource veröffentlicht wurde.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Licensing information is the text, code, or other descriptive element that identifies what license some resource is released under.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002013 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002013">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000009"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Data which are capable of realising the dispositions of findability, accessibility, interoperability, and reusability as specified in the FAIR Principles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Daten, welche die Merkmale der Auffindbarkeit, Zugänglichkeit, Interoperabilität und Wiederverwendbarkeit entsprechend der FAIR Prinzipien erfüllen können.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">See definitions of findability, accessibility, interoperability, and reusability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">FAIR data</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">FAIRe Daten</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024>FAIR data</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">FAIRe Daten</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002014 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002014">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001017"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A digital system which, when processing data, is capable of realising - simultaneously or separately - the dispositions of findability, accessibility, interoperability, and reusability as specified in the FAIR Principles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein digitales System, das bei der Verarbeitung von Daten - gleichzeitig oder nacheinander - die Merkmale der Auffindbarkeit, Zugänglichkeit, Interoperabilität und der Wiederverwendbarkeit, so wie sie in denn FAIR Prinzipien spezifiziert sind, erfüllen kann.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">FAIRes digitales System</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">See definitions of findability, accessibility, interoperability, and reusability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">FAIR digital system</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">FAIR digitales System</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A process during which some entity is modified such that it meets the requirements listed in a standard specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Prozess, in dem eine Entität so verändert wird, dass sie die Kriterien, die einer Standardspezifikation aufgeführt sind, erfüllt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Standardisierung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardisation</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization process</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The outputs of a successful standardisation process are said to be standardised or compliant to a standard.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Standard Implementierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">standards implementation process</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Standard Implementierungen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">standards implementation processes</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Standard Implementierung</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">standards implementation process</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002016 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002016">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An entity which is used as a reference, model, or example to determine membership in a set or a type.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Entität, die als Muster, Referenz oder Beispiel verwendet wird, um die Zugehörigkeit zu einer Menge oder einem Typ festzulegen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/standard"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An entity which serves as a standard for a type also meets the criteria in a standard specification for that type. A standard could be a metadata schema, a mapping/crosswalk, a data set, a model, a technical part etc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Standard</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">standard</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Standards</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">standards</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Standard</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">standard</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002018 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002018">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A process during which standard specifications (1) are developed based on the consensus of different parties and (2) are then used in a standards implementation process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Prozess, bei dem entweder (1) Standardspezifikationen auf der Grundlage eines Konsenses zwischen verschiedenen Parteien entwickelt werden oder (2) eine Entität so verändert wird, dass sie die in einer Standardspezifikation genannten Kriterien erfüllt</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Standardisierungsprozess</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">standardisation process</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization process</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The outputs of a successful standardisation process are said to be standardised or compliant to a standard.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Standardisierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">standardisation</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Standardisierungen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">standardisations</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Standardisierung</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">standardisation</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002019 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002019">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A process during which a standard specification is created or substantially modified.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Prozess, in dem eine Standardspezifikation entwickelt oder grundlegend verändert wird. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Standardisierung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardisation</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">standardization process</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This is a part of a complete standardization process</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Standardspezifikationsentwicklung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">standard specification development</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Standardspezifikationsentwicklungen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">standard specification developments</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Standardspezifikationsentwicklung</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">standard specification development</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002020 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002020">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002021"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Reusability which inheres in data whose metadata (1) are rich, comply with community standards, are associated with detailed provenance, and include links to a clear and accessible data usage license, and (2) are used - in whole or in part - to facilitate multiple, valid, and authorised uses of that data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Wiederverwendbarkeit von Daten, deren Metadaten (1) umfangreich sind, den gängigen Standards der jeweiligen Community entsprechen, eine detailliert dokumentierte Provenienz haben und auf eine eindeutige und zugängliche Datennutzungslizenz verweisen, und (2) - ganz oder teilweise - dazu verwendet werden, eine mehrfache, korrekte und autorisierte Nutzung dieser Daten zu ermöglichen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Wiederverwendbarkeit entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reusability according to the FAIR principles</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten zur Wiederverwendung, das davon abhängt, wie umfangreich sie mit exakten, standardisierten Metadaten, einschließlich Informationen zur Lizenz und Provenienz, beschrieben sind.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to be reused, based on how richly they are annotated with accurate, standardised metadata including licensing and provenance information.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002021 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002021">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition which inheres in data and which is realised when they are validly used more than once.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Veranlagung, die Daten haben können und die realisiert wird, wenn sie mehr als einmal korrekt verwendet werden. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This definition is for the reusability of data in a general sense. A more specific situation applies to reusability according to the FAIR principles which is defined elsewhere. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Wiederverwendbarkeit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reusability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten, einfach und ohne weitere Umstände mehr als einmal verwendet zu werden. Je besser diese nachgenutzt werden können, desto diverser sind die möglichen Anwendungen, zum Beispiel in anderen Systemen oder Disziplinen. </skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to be easily and readily used more than once. The more reusable data are, the more diverse the reuse of that data can be, for example in different systems or disciplines.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002022">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An objective specification which (1) defines requirements for a digital entity to be considered findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable, and (2), when fulfilled, considers that entity to be a member of the group of FAIR digital entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Ziel-Spezifikation, die (1) die Anforderungen definiert, die eine digitale Entität erfüllen muss, um als auffindbar, zugänglich, interoperabel und wiederverwendbar zu gelten und die (2) wenn diese erfüllt sind, eben jene Entität zu der Gruppe der digitalen FAIR-Entitäten zählt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">See definitions of findability, accessibility, interoperability, and reusability.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">FAIR principles</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">FAIR-Prinzipien</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A set of requirements that data properties needs to fulfill in order for the data to be findable, accessible, interoperable and re-usable. Thereby the data will be re-usable for humans and machine-agents in the long-term and thus be sustainable.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Eine Liste von Anforderungen, die Daten erfüllen müssen, um auffindbar, zugänglich, interoperabel und wiederverwendbar zu sein. Dadurch werden die Daten langfristig für Menschen und maschinelle Agenten wiederverwendbar und somit nachhaltig nutzbar.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000182"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A history which is the sum of those processes relating to the origin, ownership, custody, location, and modification of an entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Die Vorgeschichte einer Entität, die alle Vorgänge umfasst, die mit dem Ursprung, den Eigentumsrechten, der Aufbewahrung, dem Standort und der Veränderung dieser Entität zusammenhängen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://handbook.datalad.org/en/latest/glossary.html#term-provenance"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SEPIO_0000058"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provenance"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">With respect to research data this typically includes all processes and instruments that were used to generate that data, the institutions where is was generated, and the persons operating the instruments or processes. In machine learning and simulation provenance is the key to workflow documentation as software (versions) might be iterated sequentially. I.e. the change of a code downstream will significantly affect input parameters to upstream routines. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Provenienz</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">provenance</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/prov</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Die Vorgeschichte einer Entität, die alle Vorgänge umfasst, die mit dem Ursprung, den Eigentumsrechten, der Aufbewahrung, dem Standort und der Veränderung dieser Entität zusammenhängen.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The history which is the sum of those processes relating to the origin, ownership, custody, location, and modification of an entity.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002024">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000029"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Metadata which describe in whole or part the provenance of some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Metadaten, die ganz oder teilweise die Herkunft einer Entität beschreiben.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://handbook.datalad.org/en/latest/glossary.html#term-provenance"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SEPIO_0000058"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provenance"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Provenienzdaten</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">provenance data</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Provenienzmetadaten</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">provenance metadata</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/prov</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Provenienzdaten</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024>provenance data</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002025 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002025">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000039"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A record which contains data and/or information about the provenance of some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Aufzeichnung, die Daten und/oder Informationen über die Provenienz einer Entität enthält.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://handbook.datalad.org/en/latest/glossary.html#term-provenance"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SEPIO_0000058"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provenance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Provenienzaufzeichnung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">provenance record</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/prov</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Information which is about the provenance of some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Information, die die Provenienz einer Entität betreffen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://handbook.datalad.org/en/latest/glossary.html#term-provenance"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SEPIO_0000058"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provenance"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Provenance interpretation can be generated by correct and meaningful interpretation of provenance data. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Provenienzinformation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">provenance information</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/prov</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Provenienzinformationen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">provenance information</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000009"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Data which are open.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Daten, die offen sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_data"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">offene Daten</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">open data</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Data which are accessible and reusable freely and without restrictions - monetary, technical or otherwise. For this, data need to have an open license assigned and should be stored in a form and format that allows ready access and modification of the data.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Daten, die frei und ohne finanzielle, technische oder anderweitige Einschränkung zugänglich und nachnutzbar sind. Dafür muss ihnen eine freie Lizenz zugewiesen werden und die Daten sollten so strukturiert und formatiert gespeichert werden, dass der einfache Zugriff und die Änderung der Daten ermöglicht wird.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">offene Daten</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">open data</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002028 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002028">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001049"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A system which comprises elements that support the functioning or the integrity of another system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein System, das aus Elementen besteht, die die Funktionialität oder die Integrität eines anderen Systems unterstützt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C80260"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrastructure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infrastructure"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Infrastructure can include basic facilities, installations, hardware, people, and services they offer. There are different types of integrity (technical etc.). There is also the relation between functionality and integrity. Systems can function compromised integrity. In that sense, integrity might be measured on a percentage scale where 0% integrity means no functionality and 100% integrity means full functionality. Because of this scale-thing, integrity is probably a BFO-quality. TODO: Check Comment, Final approval of defintion.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Infrastruktur</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Infrastrukturen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">infrastructures</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002029 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002029">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An information technology infrastructure which supports the handling of data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Informationstechnologieinfrastruktur die die Verarbeitung von Daten unterstützt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_infrastructure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Forschungsdateninfrastruktur</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">research data infrastructure</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Actions connected to the handling of data include storage, processing, sharing, retrieval, integration, consumption, etc. This term can be broadly interpreted. This could include e.g. IT infrastructure, personnel, buildings.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Dateninfrastruktur</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Dateninfrastrukturen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">data infrastructures</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002031"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An information technology infrastructure which is only composed of digital assets.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Informationstechnologieinfrastruktur, die nur aus digitalen Ressourcen besteht. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://casrai.org/term/digital-infrastructure/"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Digital assets can be e.g. core data sets or proprietary data. TODO: Create definition for digital asset. First draft: digital entity which has a known value.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">digital infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">digtiale Infrastruktur</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An infrastructure which is composed of hardware, software, or other digital assets.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Infrastruktur, die aus Software, Hardware oder anderen digitalen Ressourcen besteht. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://casrai.org/term/digital-infrastructure/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">IT infrastructure</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">IT-Infrastruktur</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Digital assets can be e.g. core data sets or proprietary data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Informationstechnologieinfrastruktur</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">information technology infrastructure</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition of data which is realised when that data is retrieved.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Eigenschaft von Daten, die mit deren Abrufen realisiert wird. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_access"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.techopedia.com/definition/26929/data-access"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Erreichbarkeit</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">availability</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Der Prozess des Datenabrufens kann ein oder mehrere digitale Systeme und deren Interaktion beinhalten.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of accessing may include one or more digital systems and their interaction.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Zugänglichkeit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">accessibility</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten, diese abzurufen und auf diese zuzugreifen.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to be retrieved and accessed.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Zugänglichkeit</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">accessibility</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An accessibility which is realised when data and related metadata can be retrieved (1) using a standardized, open, free, and universally implementable communications protocol, (2) by dereferencing that data&apos;s globally unique and persistent identifier, and when (3) the retrieval of related metadata is permanently possible.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Zugänglichkeit, die realisiert wird, wenn Daten und zugehörige Metadaten (1) über ein standardisiertes, offenes, kostenloses und universell implementierbares Kommunikationsprotokoll, (2) durch Dereferenzierung eines weltweit eindeutigen und dauerhaften Identifikators dieser Daten abgerufen werden können und wenn (3) das Abfragen der zugehörigen Metadaten dauerhaft möglich ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Erreichbarkeit im Sinne der FAIR Prinzipien</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">availability</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Data which is only accessible to a few agents (e.g. those with access rights) can adhere to the FAIR principles. Further, data can be lost or deleted while the metadata is still accessible (e.g. as with a tombstone metadata record); in this case, the metadata is accessible, while the data is not.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Zugänglichkeit entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">accessibility according to the FAIR principles</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten oder Metadaten, auf sie durch ein standardisiertes Protokoll und das Auflösen eines weltweit eindeutigen Identifikators zuzugreifen.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data or metadata to be retrieved through a standardised protocol by resolving a globally unique identifier.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">Zugänglichkeit entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">accessibility according to the FAIR principles</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition which inheres in structured data and which is realised when a machine accesses and processes that data without human intervention or distortion of any semantic content.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Veranlagung von strukturierten Daten, die realisiert wird, wenn eine Maschine auf die Daten ohne die Beteiligung von Menschen zugreifen und sie verarbeiten kann, ohne ihren semantischen Inhalt zu verfälschen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://opendatahandbook.org/glossary/en/terms/machine-readable/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computer-readable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computerlesbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">machine-readable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">machinenlesbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">There are different depths of machine-readability, e.g. a machine with a PDF reader program can read enough content of a PDF to understand how to open and display the file contents. Depending on the agent and the data, different elements in the data may be informative. Depending on the file format, data will be readable for a larger share of existing machines.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Maschinenlesbarkeit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">machine-readability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten, alle ihnen innewohnenden Informationen automatisch auszulesen.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to read all inherent information of that data automatically.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">machine-readable</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">maschinenlesbar</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition which inheres in structured data and which is realised when a machine reads that data and performs an action directed or informed by its content.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Veranlagung von strukturierten Daten, die realisiert wird, wenn eine Maschine die Daten liest und eine Maßnahme ergreift, die vom Inhalt gesteuert wird oder darauf basiert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.i-scoop.eu/big-data-action-value-context/data-actionable/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computer-actionable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computerverarbeitbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computerverwertbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">machine-actionable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">maschinenverarbeitbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">maschinenverwertbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The disposition is somewhat orthogonal to how deeply the machine understands the information because the machine can completely understand the content without being able to do anything about it, while it would also be possible for the machine to be able to read only a small part of the data and act upon only that part without being able to read the rest of the data. If a machine cannot read data and performs an action (e.g. closes software, produces a warning), this is not due to the machine-actionability of the data, but to a pre-programmed response for non-readable (and thus non-actionable) data in the machine.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Maschinenverarbeitbarkeit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">machine-actionability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten, von einem Computer verarbeitet und verstanden zu werden.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to be processed and understood by a computer.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">machine-actionable</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">maschinenverarbeitbar</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00004005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition which inheres in a concretisation of data and which is realised when that data can be accurately translated into another concretisation and passed through components of a machine.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Veranlagung einer Daten-Konkretisierung, die realisiert wird, wenn die Daten fehlerfrei in eine andere Konkretisierung überführt und an andere Komponenten einer Maschine übergeben werden können.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_access"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computer-openable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">computer-operable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">computeroperabel</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">machine-openable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">machine-operable</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">maschinenoperabel</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">maschinenverarbeitbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">maschinenöffenbar</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Die Veranlagung betrifft die Konkretisierung der Daten, d.h. die Form, in der sie gespeichert sind. Alle Daten sind maschinen-operabel mit einer geeigneten Maschine, welche die Daten von welcher Konkretisierung oder welchem Medium auch immer in eine andere Konkretisierung kopieren kann, wobei die Bedeutung der Daten erhalten bleibt. Eine Datenoperabilität kann unabhängig von der Art der Speicherung erfolgen (digital, magnetisch, Lochkarten). Im Einzelnen erfordert eine Datenbearbeitung zunächst deren Erfassen, beispielsweise detektiert eine Kamera beim Fotografieren zunächst Bilddaten über die Lichtstrahlen. In gleicher Weise, müssen Daten im Speicher erst detektiert werden, bevor sie bearbeitet werden können. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The disposition is really in the concretisation of the data, i.e. how it is stored. Any data is machine-operable with the right machine which is capable of copying the data (from whatever its concretisation or medium) to another while maintaining its representational value. Machine-operability can apply to data recorded in any way (digital, magnet, punchcards). In even more detail, the processing of data always requires that it is first detected, e.g. a camera taking a picture first detects image data in the observed light rays. Similarly, data stored in memory is being detected before it is processed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Maschinenoperabelität</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">machine-operability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential von Daten, so gelesen zu werden, wie es beabsichtigt ist.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of data to be read as intended.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">machine-operable</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">maschinen-operabel</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which a device is adjusted to produce measurements which correspond to expected values or intervals.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Gerät so eingestellt wird, dass es Messdaten in Relation zu erwarteten Werten generiert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Kalibrierung</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">calibration</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of device calibration is carried out by either 1) measuring a set of reference materials with known properties with the device or, 2) by using a second device to measure the behavior or properties of the device.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class focusses on measurements for the moment and does not consider entities like models. In the future we will consider this issue and the relation beween calibration and parametrization.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Kalibrierungsprozess</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">calibration process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007022"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in a signifier, and is realised when that signifier falsely represents the existence, identity, or properties of some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">TODO</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Misinformation does not necessarily rely on an intent to mislead or misinform.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Fehlinformationsrolle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">misinformation role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005003">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006036"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005002"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006036"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00005002"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A generically dependent continuant which realises a misinformation role.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein generisch abhängiges Kontinuum, das eine Fehlinformationrolle umsetzt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Fehlinformation</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">misinformative data</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Misinformation is generated due to innacurate interpretation of data or other signifiers. This need not be intentional.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">misinformation</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Any sign, symbol, or data which inaccurately represents the existence, identity, or properties (i.e. provides misinformation about) of an entity.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000114"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data format which (1) is open, (2) established as a standard and (3) is based on the JavaScript Programming Language Standard ECMA-262 3rd Edition, and (4) whose rules are published on www.json.org.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Format für Daten, welches (1) offen ist, (2) als Standard etabliert ist, (3) auf dem JavaScript Programming Language Standard ECMA-262 3rd Edition basiert und (4) dessen Regeln auf www.json.org veröffentlicht sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:OMO_0003012 xml:lang="de">JSON</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <obo:OMO_0003012 xml:lang="en">JSON</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.json.org/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">JSON specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">JavaScript object notation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">JavaScript object notation specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">JSON is a language-independent data format that facilitates data storage and exchange based on a human-readable format. It was derived from JavaScript, but many modern programming languages include code to generate and parse JSON-format data. JSON filenames use the extension .json. JSON Schema specifies a JSON-based format to define the structure of JSON data to validate JSON files. This could be an instance rather than a class during implementation in OWL.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">JavaScript Object Notation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">JavaScript Object Notation</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is an open standard data interchange format that uses human-readable text to store and transmit data objects. JSON usually consists of attribute–value pairs and is language-independent. Many modern programming languages include code to generate and parse JSON-format data. JSON filenames use the extension .json.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) ist ein offenes Datenaustauschformat in menschenlesbarer Textform, um Datenobjekte zu speichern und zu übertragen. JSON besteht meistens aus Attribut-Wert-Paaren bestehen und ist sprachunabhängig. Viele moderne Programmiersprachen enthalten Code zum Generieren und Parsen von Daten im JSON-Format. JSON-Dateinamen verwenden die Erweiterung .json.</skos:note>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">JavaScript Object Notation</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">JavaScript Object Notation</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A schema that is written in accordance with the JSON Schema specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Schema, das entsprechend der JSON Schema Spezifikationen geschrieben ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A template that is constructed according to the JSON-Schema specifications, shows how (meta)data is to be structured and allows for validating entered (meta)data according to the template.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Eine Vorlage, die entsprechend den JSON Schema Spezifikationen erstellt wurde, zeigt wie (Meta)Daten strukturiert werden müssen und es erlaubt engegebene (Meta)Daten zu validieren.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">JSON Schema is written in JSON for defining the structure of JSON documents. This might be implemented as an instance of the class schema.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">JSON Schema</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">JSON schema</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">JSON Schema</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">JSON schema</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">CAPTCHA tests</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">fingerprints</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">logging in to a system</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which one or more properties of an entity are confirmed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplannter Prozess, bei dem eine oder mehrere Eigenschaften einer Entität bestätigt werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authentication"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">In contrast with identification, the act of indicating a person or thing&apos;s identity, authentication is the process of verifying that identity.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Authentifizierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">authentication</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006004">
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">OBSOLETE A specification which defines the requirements that must be met in order for code to be considered a member of JSON Schema</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">OBSOLETE Eine Spezifikation, welche Anforderungen definiert, die erfüllt sein müssen, damit Code als Teil der Klasse JSON-Schema betrachtet werden kann.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">JSON</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="en">JSON</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">JSON schema</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">JSON schema</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Converted to an instance of specification.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The &quot;application/schema+json&quot; media type is likely equivalent to HDO&apos;s &quot;abstract data type&quot;, a JSON-based format for describing the structure of JSON data. This term will likely be implemented as an instance of the term &quot;abstract data type&quot;, &quot;specification&quot;, or &quot;programming language specification&quot; when in OWL. TODO: See discussion in GitLab !81</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">obsolete JSON Schema</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete JSON Schema</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="de">JSON Schema</hob:HDO_00001026>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">JSON Schema</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which the rights to access some resource within a system are given to some agent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem ein Agent Zugriffsrechte zu einer Ressource in einem System erhält.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Genehmigung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/authorization"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authorization"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Identifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Autorisierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">authorization</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006006 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006006">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">identification card</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which the potential identity of an agent is recognized.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem die potenzielle Identität eines Agenten erkannt wird.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/identification"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">When a user logs into a system, he provides a user ID or user name on which basis the user is recognized and its identity is determined. This identity is authenticated based on a provided password or biometrics. Thus, identity authentication is the verification of identification.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Identifizierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">identification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006007 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006007">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A entity which realises an agent role.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Entität die die Rolle eines Agents einnimmt</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For now we choose to place this as a subclass of entity as there are some classes in our hieararchy above continuant that could also be acting as agents. Once the hierarchy is clearned up, we can re-discuss and consider moving this class to continuant.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Agent</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">agent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006008 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006008">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000114"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data format which (1) is open, (2) established as a standard, (3) is based on W3C recommendation (Extensible Markup Language (XML) 1.0 Fifth Edition), and (4) whose rules are published on https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datenformat, das (1) offen ist, (2) als Standard etabliert ist, (3) auf der W3C-Empfehlung (Extensible Markup Language (XML) 1.0 Fifth Edition) beruht und (4) dessen Regeln auf https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/ veröffentlicht sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:OMO_0003012>XML</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/TR/xml/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://aws.amazon.com/what-is/xml/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Extensible Markup Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Extensible Markup Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Extensible markup language Spezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Extensible markup language specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">XML Spezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">XML specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The main purpose of XML is the serialization, i.e. storing, transmitting, and reconstructing arbitrary data in a format that is both human- and machine-readable. It is a markup language and file format.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">XML</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">XML</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">Extensible Markup Language (XML) is a markup language (without predefined tags to use). It is used as a data format for storing, transmitting, and reconstructing data.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Extensible Markup Language (XML) ist eine Markup Language (ohne vordefinierte Tags zu verwenden). Sie wird als Datenformat zum Speichern, Übertragen und Rekonstruieren von Daten verwendet.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006009 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006009">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A schema which is written in accordance with the XML specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Schema, dass in Übereinstimmung mit der XML Spezifikation erstellt wurde.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:OMO_0003012>XSD</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML_Schema_(W3C)"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/XML/Schema"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Extensible markup language Schema</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Extensible markup language Schema</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class gathers individuals that refer to specific schemas&quot; (can be deleted at a later stage / when in use)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">XML Schema</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">XML schema</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A schema which specifies how the elements in an XML document are structured. Therefore, it can be used to assure that an XML document adheres to a specific structure.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Ein Schema, das angibt, wie die Elemente in einem XML-Dokument strukturiert sind. Es kann daher verwendet werden, um sicherzustellen, dass ein XML-Dokument eine bestimmte Struktur einhält.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006010 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006010">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000114"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data format which (1) uses the data format JSON and, (2) adds rules published on https://json-schema.org/specification, to define schemas.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Format für Daten, das (1) unter Verwendung des Datenformats JSON geschrieben ist und (2) diese Regeln um die auf https://json-schema.org/specification veröffentlichten Regeln erweitert um Schemas zu defineren.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://json-schema.org/"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">JSON Schema Spezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">JSON Schema specification</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A specification which enables the creation of data schemas according to JSON data format to ensure consistency, validity, and interoperability of JSON records at scale.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006011 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006011">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000114"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data format which (1) is open, (2) established as a standard and (3) whose rules are published on https://yaml.org/spec/.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datenformat, das (1) offen ist, (2) als Standard etabliert ist und (3) dessen Regeln auf https://yaml.org/spec/ veröffentlicht werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://yaml.org/spec/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">YAML specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Yet Another Markup Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Yet Another Markup Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">YAML</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">YAML</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006012 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006012">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A file which conforms to JSON format.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">JSON file</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006013 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006013">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A file which conforms to XML format.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">XML file</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006014 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006014">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000114"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data format which (1) defines the structure of data used to represent rich and complex knowledge about things and their relations, (2) is established as a standard, (3) is based on the W3C recommendation (OWL Web Ontology Language Reference), whose rules are published on https://www.w3.org/TR/owl-ref/.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datenformat, das (1) die Struktur von Daten definiert, die verwendet werden, um umfangreiches und komplexes Wissen über Dinge und ihre Beziehungen darzustellen, (2) als Standard etabliert ist, (3) auf der W3C-Empfehlung (OWL Web Ontology Language Reference) basiert, deren Regeln auf https://www.w3.org/TR/owl-ref/ veröffentlicht sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:OMO_0003012>OWL</obo:OMO_0003012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_Ontology_Language"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/OWL/"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">OWL Spezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">OWL specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Web Ontolgoy Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Web Ontology Language</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Web Ontology Language Spezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Web Ontology Language specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">OWL DL</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">OWL Full</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">OWL Lite</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">OWL2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">OWL is typically used to generate ontologies (i.e. formalise relations between entities). OWL is built on top of RDF and RDFs and is part of W3C’s Semantic Web technologies.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">OWL</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">OWL is a data format used to build ontologies. Those formalising relations between entities to create rich context for data.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A hardware which converts some energy related to a signifier to electrical signals.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Hardware, welche Energie mit Bezug zu einem Zeichen in elektrische Signale umwandelt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For some sensors, the output may already be digital signals and/or data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Sensor</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sensor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006016 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006016">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000039"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A record which comprises metadata.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datensatz, der Metadaten enthält.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/metadata-record"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Metadatensatz</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">metadata record</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006017 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006017">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Software which is proprietary.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Software, die proprietär ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">proprietary software</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">proprietäre Software</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006018 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006018">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001013"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Technologie, die digital ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Technology which is digital.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Digital technology</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Digitale Technologie</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006019 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006019">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Structured data which has structuredness conforming to a triple specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Strukturierte Daten, deren Strukturiertheit einer Triple-Spezifikation entspricht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">RDF Triple</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">RDF triple</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Semantisches Triple</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">semantic triple</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Tripel</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">triple</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006020 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006020">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000106"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A database management system which supports the interaction with triples.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Datenbank-Management-System, welches die Interaktion mit Tripeln unterstützt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">RDF Store</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">RDF store</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Tripel Store</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">triple store</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006021 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006021">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A list whose elements are curated by one or more entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Liste, deren Elemente durch eine oder mehrere Entitäten kuratiert werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Kontrollierte Liste</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">controlled list</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006022">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in an continuant and is realised when that continuant acts upon some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle, die einer Entität innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn diese Entität auf eine Entität einwirkt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">agent role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006007"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An agent which is a person.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Agent, der eine Person ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">human agent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006024">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006007"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An agent which is a software.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Agent der eine Software ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">machine agent</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">We note that any software upon onto other entity during operation and is therefore by design an agent. In data management, a machine agent or a software agent is commonly referred to when a software acts independently and or upon a system that is not its own.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">software agent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006025 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006025">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Information which identifies the data type of some data based on data typing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Information, die den Datentyp von Daten auf Basis einer Datentypisierung identifiziert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datentypinformation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data type information</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in a continuant and is realised when this continuant increases the efficiency of a planned process or extend its range of effect.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle, die einem Continuant innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn dieses Continuant die Effizienz eines geplanten Prozesses erhöht oder dessen Wirkungsbereich erweitert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tool role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001033"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Knowledge which pertains to an entity and relates it to a glyph, string or other representational entity in order to refer to it.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Wissen, das sich auf eine Entität bezieht und sie mit einer Glyphe, einer Zeichenkette oder einer anderen repräsentativen Entität in Verbindung bringt, um auf sie zu verweisen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/meaning"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/semantics"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">Meaning</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Unambiguous semantics are achieved &quot;in use&quot; or through established context. This can be the use of a word within a sentence where that word is given context by the grammar and other words in that sentence. That may also be by using formalising relations in &quot;semantic artefacts&quot; such as ontologies, which use glyphs or string to label classes and establish relations between one another.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Semantik</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">semantics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Structured data which encodes semantic relations between entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Strukturierte Daten, die semantische Beziehungen zwischen Entitäten kodieren.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The encoded relations might be between entities which are represented by words or glyps.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">semantic artefact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">semantischer Artefakt</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006029 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006029">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001013"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Technologie, die die Kodierung und den Austausch von semantischen Beziehungen ermöglicht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Technology which enables the encoding and exchange of semantic relations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Semantische Technologien</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">semantic technology</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006036"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006031"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An entity which realises a data storage role.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Entität, die eine Datenspeicher-Rolle realisiert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenspeicher</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data store</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in an entity and is realised when this entity retains a concretization of data on hardware over time in a planned process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle, die einer Entität innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn diese Entität in einem geplanten Prozess über einen gewissen Zeitraum die Konkretisierung von Daten auf Hardware speichert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">&quot;A concretisation of some data&quot; can be read as &quot;a copy of some data&quot;: the concretisation in the definition refers to data being a generally dependent continuant, which can have multiple concretisations at a time. If the here mentioned concretisation in a given data store seizes to exist, the data might still exist elsewhere.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The data storage role does not necessarily include formalised data maintenance or defined data governance. We note however, that both are beneficial for a successful long-term preservation of data within a data store. An entity which fulfils the data storage role in one process might also fulfil the data source role in another process - i.e. when making the stored data accessible for e.g. harvesting or download.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data storage role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006032 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006032">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which a concretization of data is retained for a defined amount of time in a data store.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem eine Konkretisierung von Daten für eine bestimmte Zeit in einem Datenspeicher aufbewahrt wird.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Regarding the term &quot;concretization&quot; in the definition please see comment in HDO_00006031 &quot;data storage role&quot;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenspeicherung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data storing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006072 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006072">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000108"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A digital repository which is used to define and describe data types in an arbitrary granularity and to assign persistent identifiers to these types.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein digitales Repository, welches dazu verwendet wird Datentypen in beliebiger Granularität zu definieren und zu beschreiben und diesen Typen persistente Identifikatoren zuzuweisen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://helmholtz-metadaten.de/storage/471/UseCase-Flyer_DTR.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Registry für Datentypen</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data type registry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006073 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006073">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A specification which defines the rules for accessing and interacting with objects in a digital environment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation, die die Regeln für den Zugriff und die Interaktion mit digitalen Objekten in deren Umgebung definiert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Access-Protokoll</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">access protocol</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006084 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006084">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A schema which describes the structure of a metadata record of a digital resource.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Schema welches die Struktur von Metadateneinträgen einer digitalen resource beschreibt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Informationsprofil</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">information profile</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006085 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006085">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001036"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006084"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An information profile which only structures the metadata deemed to be essential for a given purpose.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein Informationsprofil, welches die für einen bestimmten Vorgang als essentiell eingestuften Metadaten strukturiert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This definition is intentionally generic and broad - what is considered &quot;core&quot; information can vary dramatically based on application contexts and stakeholder groups. Subclasses and instances of this class can be created for particular purposes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Kernel Informationsprofil</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">kernel information profile</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006088 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A concept which is used to denote the subject matter an entity is about.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A concept which is used to denote the subject matter of an entity and is part of a controlled vocabulary.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A concept which is used to signify the subject matter of an entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A concept within a controlled vocabulary which can be used as a topic of a Digital Object.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The class was introduced to be able to represent the topic that a digital object is about.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">topic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006091 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006091">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006088"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006090"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002001"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A topic which  belongs to a controlled vocabulary and represents the subject matter of a FAIR digital object.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The class is introduced to be able to represent the topic that a digital object is about.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">FAIR digital object topic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A material entity which is a whole or part of an electronic system that 1) executes commands, and/or 2) processes signals in digital or analogue form.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine materielle Entität, die als Ganzes oder als Teil eines  elektronisches System fungiert das  Befehle oder Anweisungen zur Verarbeitung von Signalen in digitaler oder analoger Form ausführt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Computer Hardware</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">computer hardware</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">We acknowledge that the term hardware is often used with respect to computer components. WIthin the scope of HDO we use this class in a wider sense to be able to also accomodate laboratory hardware. In the future more specific subclasses such as computer hardware could be created to accomodate classes like GPU, CPU or HDD. 

We also acknowledge the use of the term hardware for tools and tooling but find this meaning to be outside of the HDO scope.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Wir erkennen an, dass der Begriff Hardware oft in Bezug auf Computerkomponenten verwendet wird. Im Rahmen von HDO verwenden wir diese Klasse in einem weiteren Sinne, um auch Laborhardware zu berücksichtigen. In Zukunft könnten spezifischere Unterklassen wie Computer-Hardware geschaffen werden, um auch Klassen wie GPU, CPU oder HDD zu berücksichtigen.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Hardware</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hardware</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process through which information about an entity is inferred, extracted from data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, durch den Informationen über eine Entität aus Daten abgeleitet werden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Statistik</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">statistics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The output of the analysis process may either be a transformed version of the input data or created de novo during the analysis process in both cases it need to serve an information role. We also consider signifiers to be a possible output of data analysis. This is described by the following example.

During the MRI the magnetic signals are measured. These are analyzed from an image that can be considered data. Also it can be considered a signifier as only further analysis by a doctor (or a machine agent) a tissue damage can be diagnosed. In any case the output has to serve an information role for the process to be considered data analysis. In this example the input data is transformed during the analysis process in order to become informative.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenanalyse</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data analysis</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200000</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">Datenanalysen</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">data analyses</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in a generically dependent continuant and is realized when that generically dependent continuant indicates the existence, identity, properties, or behaviours of another entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Eine Rolle, die einer Entität innewohnt und die verwirklicht wird, wenn diese Entität als repräsentativ für eine andere interpretiert wird</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Signalisierungrolle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">signifier role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006036"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007003"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006036"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007003"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A generically dependent continuant which realizes a signifier role.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein generisch abhängiges Kontinuum, das eine Signifier-Rolle umsetzt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dce:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3949-818X"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Zeichen einer Qualität</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">signifier of a quality</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">symbol</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">indicator</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">representational entity</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">sign</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">signal</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Example: A fingerprint on a pane of glass that indicates an individual which may have touched the glass at some point in time.

In the example, note that the fingerprint itself is not the signifier but realizes the signifier role. The signifier depends on the entity that realizes the signifier role (i.e. the fingerprint) and the entity performing the interpretation (i.e putting the signifier in relation to previous experience) leading to the conclusion that the fingerprint might indicate the interaction of an individual with the pane of glass.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Example: a symbol for dangerous goods on a sticker placed on e.g. trucks or on bottles in a laboratory, which indicates a property of the contained substance (i.e. acidic,  flammable).

In the example, note that the physically printed symbol for dangerous goods itself is not the signifier but realizes the signifier role. The signifier depends on the entity that realizes the signifier role (i.e. the symbol on the sticker) and the entity performing the interpretation (i.e putting the signifier in relation to previous experience) leading to the conclusion that the symbol on the sticker might indicate the presence of a dangerous substrance.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Example: smoke that indicates the presence of a combustion process.

In the example, note that the smoke itself is not the signifier but realizes the signifier role. The signifier depends on the entity that realizes the signifier role (i.e. the smoke) and the entity performing the interpretation (i.e putting the signifier in relation to previous experience) leading to the conclusion that the smoke might indicate the presence of a fire.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The generic dependence of a signifier is on the entity that realizes the signifier role, not on the entity which is signified.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The term &apos;indicates&apos; in the definition implies an interpretation process which will have as output either information or mis-information.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Zeichen</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">signifier</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3949-818X"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Jos Lehmann</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A quality which inheres in a bearer by virtue of the variation in that bearer&apos;s qualities or parts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Eigenschaft die ein Träger oder einer Trägerin, aufgrund der Veränderlichkeit seiner oder ihrer Eigenschaften oder Teile hat.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_content"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Shannon entropy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">information content</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">surprisal</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">information</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For example, the self-information of the string &quot;AAAAAAA&quot; is null (no variation), while that of the string &quot;ABRPGE3&quot; is high. This is aligned to the notion of Shannon entropy, which is often derived from the probability of an event occuring: a 100% chance of an event occuring corresponds to zero information (no variation).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class is distinct from &quot;information&quot; in the more colloquial sense (i.e. informative content), which we express in HDO&apos;s &quot;information role&quot;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">self-information</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007008 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007008">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">OBSOLETE A generically dependent continuant which is composed of at least two datum instances.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:consider rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000009"/>
        <oboInOwl:consider rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001037"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Colloquially, &quot;data&quot; is sometimes used to refer to anything that can be perceived. Here, however, we require that those sense-impressions are encoded such that they can be recorded, transmitted, and understood by at least one agent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Now inlcuded as the plural of datum.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">We have created this class as most digital entities involve &apos;data&apos; rather than a singular datum. How to position this at the BFO upper-level is still under discussion. The definition of data as a generically dependent continuant which is composed of at least two datum instances is correct, however some intervening class expressing a collection of generically dependent continuants may be useful in future (parallel to BFO:&apos;object aggregate&apos;).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete data</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">A collection of signs, signals, symbols, or other signifiers (e.g. numbers, characters in a known alphabet, strings with an assigned meaning, known graphical symbols, viewable images) which (1) represent one or more entities or their properties and (2) have been recorded in a manner that allows their transmission.

An example: A collection of numbers which represent radio waves and have been recorded on a hard drive. The numbers are the signs mentioned above. The radio waves are also signals but not the ones mentioned above.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007010 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007010">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disposition which inheres in an agent and which is realised when that agent successfully coordinates one or more of its operations with those of another agent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Veranlagung eines Akteurs, die realisiert wird, wenn dieser Akteur erfolgreich mit einem anderen Akteur kommuniziert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C142381"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://wordnetweb.princeton.edu/perl/webwn?o2=&amp;o0=1&amp;o8=1&amp;o1=1&amp;o7=&amp;o5=&amp;o9=&amp;o6=&amp;o3=&amp;o4=&amp;s=interoperability&amp;h=0&amp;j=0#c"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/interoperability"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Interoperation implies that all participating agents are able to complete a joint operation based on the information they exchange. We note that communication is an essential part of the coordination of operations mentioned in the definition. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Interoperabilität</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">interoperability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential zweier verschiedener Akteure zusammenzuarbeiten. Ein Akteur kann ein Mensch oder eine Maschine sein. </skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of two different agents to work together. An agent may be a human or a machine.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007011 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007011">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007010"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Interoperability which is realised when the involved agents use one or more formal languages for knowledge representation to coordinate their operations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Interoperabilität, die realisiert wird, wenn die beteiligten Akteure eine formale Sprache für Wissensrepräsentation benutzen um ihre Operationen zu koordinieren.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C142682"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Semantische Interoperabilität</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">semantic interoperability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential zweier verschiedener Akteure zusammenzuarbeiten, indem sie Informationen austauschen, die mithilfe einer eindeutig definierten Terminologie strukturiert sind.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of agents to coordinate their activity by referencing a common understanding or system of knowledge. </skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007012 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007012">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007010"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine semantische Interoperabilitätsveranlagung, die realisiert wird, wenn die formalen Sprachen für Wissensrepräsentation (1) breit anwendbar sind, (2) FAIR kodiert sind und (3) benutzt werden um Beziehungen zu anderen (Meta)Daten zu qualifizieren. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Semantic interoperability which is realised when the formal languages for knowledge representation are (1) broadly applicable, (2) their encodings are FAIR, and (3) they are used to qualify references to other (meta)data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">&quot;Broadly applicable&quot; as used in the I1 subprinciple of the FAIR principles is somewhat ambiguous. It may suggest either that the language for knowledge representation is broadly applied or that it can be broadly applied. In HMC we would favor that such languages are well used by at least the stakeholder communities (i.e. are a de facto standard) and that their technical quality allows even broader use. As opposed to the FAIR principles, our definitions do not directly talk about (meta)data but describe it indirectly through the inter-agent communication. Part of our rationale was that data by itself is not an agent and thus cannot interoperate with someone or something as might be assumed by the wording of the FAIR principles.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Interoperabilität entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">interoperability according to the FAIR principles</rdfs:label>
        <skos:note xml:lang="de">Das Potential zweier verschiedener Akteure zusammenzuarbeiten, indem sie Informationen austauschen, die mit einer eindeutig definierten und den FAIR-Prinzipien folgenden Terminologie strukturiert sind.</skos:note>
        <skos:note xml:lang="en">The potential of agents to work together by referencing a digitised terminology that follows the FAIR principles.</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in an entity and is realised when this entity allows data to be accessed in a planned process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle, die einer Entität innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn diese Entität in einem geplanten Prozess den Zugriff auf Daten ermöglicht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The accessed data is in fact a concretization of data. Please see comment in HDO_00006031 &quot;data storage role&quot;</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The data that is being made accessible by a data source might have been stored by that entity (then this entity has fulfilled a data storage role before). It might also be output of a measurement process (HDO_00001070) by scientific devices such as instruments or sensors.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenquellenrolle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data source role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007022">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in a generally dependent continuant, and is realised when that generally dependent continuant reduces uncertainty about the existence, identity, or properties of the entity it represents.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle die einem generally dependent continuant innewohnt, und die realisiert wird, wenn dieses generally dependent continuant die Ungewissheit bezüglich der Existenz, Identität oder der Eigenschaften einer Entität die es repräsentiert, verringert.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Informations Rolle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">information role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000009"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Data which encode a signifier.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Daten, die ein Zeichen kodieren.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">qualitative Daten</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">qualitative data</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="de">qualitative Daten</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">qualitative data</hob:HDO_00001024>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007024">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">OBSOLETE A signifier which is the output of a qualification process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">OBSOLETE Ein Zeichen, das das Ergebnis eines Qualifizierungsprozesses ist.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007004"/>
        <rdfs:comment>the class is equivalent to existing class `signifier`</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">obsolete Zeichen einer Eigenschaft</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete signifier of a quality</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A specification which pertains to the structuredness of one or more data sets.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation, die die Strukturiertheit von ein oder mehreren Datensätzen betrifft.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://edamontology.org/format_1915"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C42761"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_data_type"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_format"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.duden.de/rechtschreibung/Struktur"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/data%20structure"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Datenstruktur</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Datenstrukturspezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">data structure</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The data structure specificaiton defines how parts or components of a data set are arranged and relate to each other. It does not comprise information regarding the syntax that data is represented in (data format) or the serialization of how that data is stored within a system (file format).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datenstrukturspezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data structure specification</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000005"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires a data set to consist of a sequence of elements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die verlangt, dass ein Datensatz aus einer Folge von Elementen besteht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Liste</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">list</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Listenspezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">list specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires some data to consist of two elements, the first of which realizes a key role in order to find and access the other element which is a value.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Eine Datenstruktursprezifikation, die verlangt, dass Datenpaar aus zwei Elementen bestehen, von denen das erste eine Schlüsselrolle einnimmt, um das andere Element, welches einen Wert ist, zu finden und darauf zuzugreifen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Feldspezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">field specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Schlüssel-Wert Paar</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">key-value pair</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Schlüssel-Wert Paar Spezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">key-value pair specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007028 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007028">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires some data to consist of a set of key-value pairs with unique keys.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die erfordert, dass Daten aus einer Menge von Schlüssel-Wert-Paaren mit eindeutigen Schlüsseln besteht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://computersciencewiki.org/index.php/Dictionaries"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associative_array"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_(computer_science)"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Mapspezifikation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">map specification</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">Objektspezifikation</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">mapping</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">object specification</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dictionary specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007029 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007029">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires some data to consist of at least two elements, known as points or nodes, that are related with one another via relations, known as edges or links.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die erfordert, dass Daten aus mindestens zwei Elementen, bekannt als Punkte oder Knoten, bestehen, die durch Beziehungen, bekannt als Kanten oder Verbindungen, miteinander verbunden sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Graphspezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">graph specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001037"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Structured data which has structuredness conforming to a list specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Strukturierte Daten, deren Strukturiertheit einer Listenspezifikation folgt.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Liste</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">list</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007032 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007032">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00006028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Structured data which has structuredness conforming to a dictionary specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Strukturierte Daten, deren Strukturiertheit einer Wörterbuchspezifikation enspricht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associative_array"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_(computer_science)"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">map (computer science)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">object (computer science)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dictionary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007033 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007033">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007029"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A graph specification which requires the edges in a graph to be directed edges.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Graphenspezifikation, die erfordert, dass die Kanten in einem Graphen gerichtet sind.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">directed graph specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007034 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007034">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007033"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A directed graph specification which requires a directed graph data set to not contain any graphical cycles which consist of edges of the same type.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation für gerichtete Graphen, die erfordert, dass in einem Graphen keine zyklischen Strukturen mit Verbindungen des selben Typs gebildet werden dürfen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">directed acyclic graph specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007035 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007035">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A directed acyclic graph specification which requires a directed acyclic graph to be (1) used to represent knowledge about entities (represented as nodes) by relating them to one another with formalised logical relations (represented as edges), (2) logically coherent, such that it can be reasoned over and used for inference by machine agents and (3) constructed such that nodes further along in a path inherit all the semantic properties of their antecedents.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Spezifikation zu gerichteten, azyklischen Graphen, die von solchen Graphen fordert, dass sie (1) dazu verwendet werden, Wissen über Objekte zu veranschaulichen, indem die Entitäten (repräsentiert als Knoten) mit formalisierte logische Beziehungen (repräsentiert als Kanten) verbunden werden, (2) logisch kohärent sind, so dass sie von maschinellen Agenten für Begründungen und Schlussfolgerung verwendet werden können und (3) so aufgebaut sind, dass entlang eines Pfades alle Knoten die semantischen Eigenschaften der zuvor besuchten Knoten erben.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ontological graph specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007036 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007036">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007029"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A graph specification which requires a graph to use machine-actionable semantic technology to (1) describe its elements and their instances and (2) qualify the relations between them.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Graphspezifikation, für deren Erfüllung ein Graph maschinell verarbeitbare semantische Technologie verwenden muss, um (1) seine Elemente und deren Instanzen zu beschreiben und (2) die Beziehungen zwischen ihnen zu qualifizieren.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network of real-world entities — i.e. objects, events, situations, or concepts — and the relationship between them. The content of the KG is typically human- and machine-readable. The Google Knowledge Graph is an example of a large-scale knowledge graph used by Google and its services to enhance its search engine&apos;s results.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Wissensgraphspezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">knowledge graph specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007037 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007037">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires a data set to be (1) collected in a centralised manner and (2) organized in a consistent structure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die verlangt, dass Daten (1) zentral gesammelt und (2) in einer einheitlichen Struktur organisiert wurden.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Because of the close relationship between them, the term &quot;database&quot; is often used casually to refer to both a database and the database management system used to manipulate it. Here, we use the term to refer to any organised collection of data that forms the basis of some activity and the term &quot;database system&quot; to describe the combination of a database and a database management system. It is generally assumed that the organisation of data in a database will enhance efficiency of operations such as search, retrieval, update, and auditing. These actions are usually performed through a database management system.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">database specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007038 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007038">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires a data set to minimally contain (1) subject data, (2) metadata about that subject data, and (3) a globally unique identifier which, when dereferenced, allows an agent to access the data set itself.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die vorschreibt, dass ein Datensatz mindestens (1) Subjektdaten, (2) Metadaten über diese Subjektdaten und (3) einen global eindeutigen Identifier enthält, der, wenn er dereferenziert wird, Zugriff auf den Datensatz selbst ermöglicht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">digital object specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007039 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007039">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires a data set to encode a hierarchy of entities by using a consistent set of principles of relatedness.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation für deren Einhaltung die Entitäten in einem Datensatz hierarchisch angeordnet sein müssen, unter Verwendung eines einheitlichen Prinzips der Verbundenheit.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="de">taxonomy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hierarchical arrangement of entities based on how similar they are to one another. Entities deeper in the hierarchy need to retain all the properties of their ancestors. Terminologies can also be structured as a taxonomy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="de">Eine hierarchische Anordnung von Entitäten, basierend auf ihrer Ähnlichkeit untereinander. Entitäten auf niedrigeren Hierarchieebenen müssen alle Eigenschaften der ihnen in direkter Linie übergeordneten Entitäten übernehmen. Terminologien können auch als Taxonomie strukturiert sein.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">taxonomy specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007040 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007040">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001011"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A planned process during which it is determined whether the type or properties of an entity conform to a specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Ein geplanter Prozess, bei dem festgestellt wird, ob der Typ oder die Eigenschaften einer Entität mit einer Spezifikation übereinstimmen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Überprüfung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://blog.golayer.io/business/data-validation"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/validation"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_validation"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://www.nasa.gov/seh/5-4-product-validation"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Konformitätsüberprüfung</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="de">Validation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">validation process</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="de">Daten Validierung</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">data validation</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">In the context of this ontologies most types of validation will pertain to data. Some other types of validation might pertain to scientific equipment or samples however. For now we intended to keep the hierarchy light and therefore did not include a specific &quot;data validation&quot; class which we might consider in the future if instances in this class get too heterogeneous. 
Data validation is a critical aspect of data management. It ensures that data entered into a system is accurate, consistent, and meets the standards set for that specific system. A failed validation (e.g. of a metadata record against a metadata schema) would render the entity invalid and consequently it would not be a member of the validated set of entities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Validierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">validation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007041 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007041">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001036"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A validation during which it is determined whether some metadata record conforms to some metadata schema.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Validierung, bei der festgestellt wird, ob ein Metadatensatz einem Metadatenschema entspricht.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Metadatenüberprüfung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">metadata record validation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Metadatenvalidierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">metadata validation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001036"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007042 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007042">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A validation during which it is determined whether some data conforms to some data type.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Validierung, bei der festgestellt wird, ob bestimmte Daten einem bestimmten Datentyp entsprechen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym xml:lang="de">Datentypüberprüfung</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Data type validation is typically used in programming where it is assessed whether some data conforms to e.g. the rules of the data type string, boolean, list, integer or else.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Datentypvalidierung</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">data type validation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000007"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007043 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007043">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">OBSOLETE A validation during which it is determined whether some data conforms to some rules.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The rules involved in data validation can concern various aspects, e.g. correctness or structure.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>adding &apos;data validation&apos; as a class was discussed during the development of HDO v 1.0. We decided to deprecate the class for now, in order to wait and see if various types of validations end up being instantiated in the class &apos;validation&apos;. Should that be the case we would reconsider refining the hierarchy and adding &apos;data validation&apos; as a sub-class of validation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">to be depricated</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete data validation</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_10000047 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_10000047">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role which inheres in an entity and is realized when the magnitude of at least one of its qualities is used as a reference to express the magnitude of the same quality or qualities in other entities.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Rolle, die einer Entität innewohnt und realisiert wird, wenn die Größe mindestens einer ihrer Eigenschaften als Referenz verwendet wird, um die Größe der gleichen Eigenschaft oder Eigenschaften anderer Entitäten auszudrücken.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Unit"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unit_of_measurement"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">unit of measurement role</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The quality in this definition refers to physical qualities such as length, duration, weight. If qualities can be related they are neccessarily of the same physical dimension. If a unit role is realised in a process of measurement, the unit is a  unit of measurement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Einheitsrolle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">unit role</rdfs:label>
        <hob:HDO_00001024 xml:lang="en">unit roles</hob:HDO_00001024>
        <hob:HDO_00001026 xml:lang="en">unit role</hob:HDO_00001026>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/hdo.owl#triple_specification -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/hdo.owl#triple_specification">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00007025"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A data structure specification which requires structured data to consist of three elements, that describe an entities (the subject) relation (the predicate) with another entity (the object) in a fixed order.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="de">Eine Datenstrukturspezifikation, die vorschreibt, dass strukturierte Daten aus drei Elementen bestehen müssen, die die Beziehung (Prädikat) zwischen einer Entität (Subjekt) und einer anderen Entität (Objekt) in einer festen Reihenfolge beschreiben.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">We note that a triple consist of a fixed order that is subject-predicate-object.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="de">Tripel Spezifikation</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">triple specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


